# Build output. frontend/dist is embedded by go:embed but is regenerated by
# `wails build`, so it is not tracked; build/bin holds the compiled binary.
build/bin
# `make deb` stages the package tree here and writes the .deb next to it.
build/deb
# `make nsis` has Wails stage the WebView2 bootstrapper here to embed it in the
# installer. The installer itself lands in build/bin, which is ignored above.
build/windows/installer/tmp
# Wails rewrites this on every `-nsis` run from the template embedded in the tool,
# resolving the `{{.Info.*}}` placeholders against wails.json in place. It says "DO
# NOT EDIT - Generated automatically by `wails build`" for that reason, and the
# tracked form is not usable by makensis at all, so it is generated output like
# frontend/dist rather than a source file. project.nsi beside it *is* a source file:
# defines put there win over the generated ones.
build/windows/installer/wails_tools.nsh
node_modules
frontend/dist

# Wails caches the dependency hash next to package.json.
frontend/package.json.md5

# Local session/agent metadata.
.freebuff/

# The chat database lives in ~/.config/kichat, but exclude any stray copy.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.log
